From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan Yocom <630234+danyocom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:44:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] Return to the launcher when L+R+Down+B is held in a
 retail game

Holding L+R+Down+B for two seconds reboots into Pico Loader, which then
boots the launcher. This works whether or not the game implements a soft
reset of its own.

The keys are counted in the SDK interrupt dispatcher. Its final table
dispatch is the same from SDK 2 through SDK 5, so one signature covers
the retail library; the match is only used when the dispatcher's start
is nearby and its literal return address matches the relocated location.
The dispatch is replaced with a jump to patch code that performs it and
checks the keys on vblank.

The reset waits until the slot 1 lock is free and takes it, so no rom
read or save operation is interrupted on the cartridge bus, then enters
the OS_ResetSystem reboot and marks the reset parameter. Pico Loader's
arm7 recognises the marker and loads the launcher.

The patch is optional: it is skipped when the dispatcher is not found or
its code, and the reboot if the game has none, do not fit in the
remaining patch space.
